+\subsubsection{Global and Local AE-PR Guidance}
+\label{subsec:followup_weighting}
+We evaluate the $2\times2$ factorial design on Citeseer with seeds $15$--$19$ at both $5\%$ and $10\%$ structural budgets (40 completed runs). Let $G_0/G_1$ and $L_0/L_1$ denote topology-only/attribute-weighted transitions at the global and local stages, respectively. Each stage keeps its source, recurrence, iteration count, and readout fixed. Globally, the source is normalized unweighted degree, with $\alpha_g=0.15$ and 30 accumulated states including initialization. Locally, the two selected endpoints receive equal restart mass, with $\alpha_\ell=0.28$ and 60 updates, reading the final state. Thus $L_0$ is endpoint PPR, distinct from ordinary PR in the selector comparison below.
+
+These follow-ups use the graph \emph{before} the selected edge flip and freeze structural-search features at their original values. They test weighting under this controlled configuration, rather than the post-flip dependency specified by the main method. Within each global setting, the two local arms share a verified structural-action trajectory; changing global weighting may change that trajectory. All arms share the initial graph and features, attribute constraints, generation rules, and victim-training seed streams. Appendix~\ref{app:followup_details} documents the effective split, parameters, and actual attribute consumption.
+
+Fig.~\ref{fig:ae_ppr_2x2_ablation} reports mean attacked accuracy and sample standard deviation across five seeds. Both stages weighted ($G_1L_1$) attain the lowest means: $58.79\%$ at $5\%$ and $57.01\%$ at $10\%$, compared with $59.58\%$ and $57.89\%$ for $G_0L_0$. Clean accuracy is $72.85\%\pm1.41$ across the same seeds. The paired local-weighting gain is $1.31$ and $0.65$ percentage points under $G_1$, but $-0.02$ and $0.09$ under $G_0$ (Table~\ref{tab:factorial_paired}). The estimated interactions are positive, $1.33$ and $0.56$ points, but both confidence intervals include zero. Exact two-sided paired sign-flip tests with Holm correction across the ten planned contrasts yield $p\geq0.625$. Even the $5\%$ local effect under $G_1$, whose unadjusted $t$ interval barely excludes zero, has raw $p=0.0625$. These five-seed results suggest a conditional local-weighting benefit but do not establish a reliable interaction or a general advantage from global weighting.
 
